window.docContents[80].resolve({"/Induction/#Logical-Foundations--Induction___-Proof-by-Induction--More-Exercises--A-New-Tactic-Combinator":{"contents":"\n\nNew tactic combinator: t₁ <;> t₂ runs t₁, then runs t₂ on every\nsubgoal produced by t₁.\n\nexample (b : Bool) : (b || true) = true := by\n  cases b <;> rfl\nexample (b : Bool) : (b || true) = true := by\n  cases b <;> rfl\nexample (b : Bool) : (b || true) = true := by\n  cases b <;> rfl\n\n\nThis is short for:\n\nexample (b : Bool) : (b || true) = true := by\n  cases b with\n  | false => rfl\n  | true  => rfl\nexample (b : Bool) : (b || true) = true := by\n  cases b with\n  | false => rfl\n  | true  => rfl\nexample (b : Bool) : (b || true) = true := by\n  cases b with\n  | false => rfl\n  | true  => rfl\n\n\n\n\nWe can also chain <;>s.\n\nexample (b c : Bool) : (b && c) = (c && b) := by\n  cases b <;> cases c <;> rfl\nexample (b c : Bool) : (b && c) = (c && b) := by\n  cases b <;> cases c <;> rfl\nexample (b c : Bool) : (b && c) = (c && b) := by\n  cases b <;> cases c <;> rfl\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Induction: Proof by Induction\u0009More Exercises","header":"2.5.1. A New Tactic Combinator","id":"/Induction/#Logical-Foundations--Induction___-Proof-by-Induction--More-Exercises--A-New-Tactic-Combinator"}});